-- title:
--   Diffusion commutes with beam-splitter mixing on product inputs, Eq. (21)
-- statement:
--   Let $n\ge1$ and let $\rho_X,\rho_Y$ be arbitrary normalized states on the full $n$-mode bosonic Fock spaces. Their joint input is the product $\rho_X\otimes\rho_Y$; entanglement within either input is unrestricted. Let $B_\lambda$ retain the port with quadratures $\sqrt\lambda R_X+\sqrt{1-\lambda}R_Y$. Write $S$ for extended nonnegative von Neumann entropy in nats.
--
--   Let $\mathcal H_t$ be the Gaussian displacement diffusion generated by $-\tfrac14\sum_{j=1}^{2n}[R_j,[R_j,\cdot]]$, with the canonical Weyl convention. For all $t\ge0$ and $0\le\lambda\le1$,
--   $$\mathcal H_t(B_\lambda(\rho_X\otimes\rho_Y))=B_\lambda(\mathcal H_t(\rho_X)\otimes\mathcal H_t(\rho_Y)).$$
--   The same time is used in all three evolutions. This is an identity of full density operators, with no smoothness or energy restriction.
-- source:
--   Limits on classical communication from quantum entropy power inequalities, arXiv:1205.3407v2, PDF p. 7, Diffusion commutes with beam-splitter mixing on product inputs, Eq. (21)

import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Intakenext100_P62

noncomputable section

